# The same lookup through two lists at the same places: the modes and their plans are two values, which only the places
# they share tie together, and `index` finds where the mode stands among the modes. What the table says in one value,
# the shortcut says in two.

route tables.plans.timeout
step timeout/index

line entry > timeout call
line Mode·modes > timeout value
line Plan·plans > timeout value              # `plans[..].timeout`
line Mode·mode > timeout value
line Mode·modes > timeout/index value        # `index(modes, mode)`
line Mode·mode > timeout/index value
line timeout/index > timeout back            # the place, a number, goes to the lookup

home Mode·modes timeout
home Plan·plans timeout
home Mode·mode timeout

side entry left
